Don't do this feature for now, I'll do it next week: Add assert.match() / assert.notMatch() for general purpose object pattern matching (strings, instances, objects, arrays, etc.)

- Shouldnt shims/deno/vendor-types folder be generated by deno?: https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/33290

- Browser: `module.skip()` / `describe.skip()` swallows everything declared after it.
  QUnit's `QUnit.module.skip(name)` opens a module scope, so sibling tests declared
  later in the same callback get absorbed into the skipped module and reported as
  skipped instead of running. Node and Deno both run them. Visible in test/skip-test.ts:
  "normal test after skip entries still runs" is reported as skipped in the browser.
  Fix idea: register the skipped module with an empty callback and restore the previous
  QUnit module scope afterwards.
